# A member lookup through a qualifier that supplies nothing used to be compiled
# as the BARE NAME of the member, and the diagnostic then said
# `undefined variable (Foo)` — naming the attribute and never the qualifier
# that actually failed, so the message pointed at the wrong half of the line.
# It was the first wall on four html5lib files, where it read as a typo.
#
# `strings` is a Pascal RTL unit wearing a Python module's name. The companion
# test test_nilpy_bare_name_error_stays_short is the control: a genuinely bare
# undefined name must KEEP the short message, because there is no receiver to
# name and inventing one would be the same defect pointing the other way.
# bug-n-an-attribute-on-an-unresolved-import-degrades-to-a-bare-name

import strings
print(strings.Foo)
